{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "adversarial_observed_label_reversal",
  "task": "Summarize the observed raw counts for Increasing using counts.zarr, metadata.csv and task_inputs.json. Align expression columns and metadata by sample_id, and group by the supplied embryonic_age labels. Report the arithmetic mean at each of the four observed stages in stage_kinetics, in raw count units; do not replace observations with fitted or smoothed values. Order stages numerically, not lexically. Calculate temporal_score as sum(sign(next_mean-current_mean))/(number_of_stages-1), using sign(0)=0. Under this task's strict rule, is_monotonic is true only when the score is exactly +1 or -1; otherwise temporal_direction is non_monotonic, including a flat profile. Also check the rank and 2-norm condition number of the specified design; numeric_time is the numeric portion of the supplied stage label. Do not infer the answer from gene names or expression-column order. This is a descriptive synthetic-data check: no GLM fit, p-value, biological-independence assumption, causal claim or clinical conclusion is requested. Supplied grouping labels are observations, not proof of true developmental time. Write finite final_discovery.json matching answer_schema.json. Retain full numerical precision when computing means and the signed score.",
